/Alt (The six panel figure shows three heatmaps in the top row and three bar graphs in the bottom row. Panel a, a heatmap, shows a normal distribution with values from 2 to 8. Panel b, a heatmap, shows a skewed distribution with values from 1 to 4. Panel c, a heatmap, shows a long-tail distribution with values from 0.5 to 2.0. Panel d, a bar graph, corresponds to panel a, showing a normal distribution with counts peaking around 50. Panel e, a bar graph, corresponds to panel b, showing a skewed distribution with counts peaking around 40. Panel f, a bar graph, corresponds to panel c, showing a long-tail distribution with counts peaking around 60.)
