/A 1952 0 R
/Alt (The 12 panel diagram arranged in three rows of four shows sv\(X\) maps, scatter plots, bar graphs, and prediction maps. Panel a, panel e, and panel i are sv\(X\) maps. Panel a shows a grid of dots with values ranging from 1.9 to 2.1. Panel e shows a grid of dots with values ranging from 1.6 to 2.4. Panel i shows a grid of dots with values ranging from 0.5 to 1.5. Panel b, panel f, and panel j are scatter plots of Y train versus sv\(X\). In panel b, Y train decreases as sv\(X\) increases from 1.9 to 2.2. In panel f, Y train decreases as sv\(X\) increases from 1.8 to 2.4. In panel j, Y train decreases as sv\(X\) increases from 1.5 to 3.0. Panel c, panel g, and panel k are bar graphs of importance impurity for X and sv\(X\). In panel c, X has higher importance than sv\(X\). In panel g, X has higher importance than sv\(X\). In panel k, X has higher importance than sv\(X\). Panel d, panel h, and panel l are OK versus SRK prediction maps. Panel d shows predictions ranging from 3 to 7. Panel h shows predictions ranging from 1 to 3. Panel l shows predictions ranging from 0.5 to 1.5.)
/K 23
/P 36 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
