/Alt (The three panel diagram shows a workflow for singularity regression kriging model for trace element prediction in a mining region. The diagram is arranged in three rows. The first row shows data preprocessing and variable selection, followed by singularity feature engineering and trend modelling. The second row shows model validation, followed by modelling and prediction. The data preprocessing and variable selection section includes data standardisation, distance to lithology normalisation, aggregate observations, and a Zn Spearman correlation matrix. The singularity feature engineering and trend modelling section includes singularity feature construction, trend estimation, and residual kriging and prediction. The model validation section includes cross validation, sensitivity analysis, prediction comparison, uncertainty analysis, and cross section predictions. The modelling and prediction section shows a map of Zn parts per million.)
/K 1
/P 36 0 R
/Pg 19 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
