/A 2109 0 R
/Alt (The five-panel graph arranged in two rows of two heatmaps and one line graph shows sensitivity analysis for Zn and Co. Panel a, a heatmap for Zn mean R squared, displays maximum singularity scale from 10 to 25 kilometres on the vertical axis and sv threshold from 0 to 1 on the horizontal axis. Mean R squared values range from 0.327 to 0.352, with higher values in the lower left. Panel b, a heatmap for Zn mean RMSE, uses the same axes. Mean RMSE values range from 21.35 to 21.79, with lower values in the lower left. Panel c, a heatmap for Co mean R squared, uses the same axes. Mean R squared values range from 0.330 to 0.365, with higher values in the lower left. Panel d, a heatmap for Co mean RMSE, uses the same axes. Mean RMSE values range from 10.31 to 10.63, with lower values in the lower left. Panel e, a line graph, shows relative change in percentage for R squared and RMSE for Zn and Co across parameter combinations. The horizontal axis shows parameter combinations from 10 kilometres 0 to 25 kilometres 1. The vertical axis shows relative change from minus 5.0 to 5.0 percentage. For Zn, R squared change varies from minus 2.5 to 2.5 percentage, while RMSE change varies from minus 2.5 to 2.5 percentage. For Co, R squared change varies from minus 5.0 to 2.5 percentage, while RMSE change varies from minus 2.5 to 2.5 percentage. Dashed lines indicate plus or minus 5 percentage.)
/K 0
/P 36 0 R
/Pg 23 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
