/A 2112 0 R
/Alt (The 2-panel heatmap arranged side by side shows spatial predictions of trace elements zinc and cobalt across a study area. Panel a displays zinc concentration in parts per million. It contains five subpanels: SRK, OK, IDW, LM, RF, and RFK. The SRK subpanel shows a large central region of high zinc concentration, with values decreasing towards the edges. The OK subpanel shows a gradient from high concentration at the bottom right to low at the top left. The IDW, LM, RF, and RFK subpanels show similar patterns to SRK, with a central high concentration area. A vertical legend indicates zinc values from 5.4 to 110.9 parts per million. Panel b displays cobalt concentration in parts per million, with five subpanels: SRK, OK, IDW, LM, RF, and RFK. The SRK subpanel shows a central region of high cobalt concentration, with values decreasing towards the edges. The OK subpanel shows a gradient from high concentration at the bottom right to low at the top left. The IDW, LM, RF, and RFK subpanels show similar patterns to SRK, with a central high concentration area. A vertical legend indicates cobalt values from 2.0 to 65.9 parts per million. Both panels include a north arrow and a horizontal scale bar from 0 to 50 kilometres.)
/K 3
/P 36 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
