/Alt (The two-panel line graph shows predicted zinc and cobalt concentrations versus Easting. Panels are arranged vertically. Panel a, at the top, displays predicted zinc concentration in parts per million on the vertical axis, ranging from 0 to 60, against Easting in metres on the horizontal axis, ranging from 13650000 to 13750000. An inset diagram in the upper left shows a cross section with a horizontal line indicating the measurement path. Six models are plotted: OK, IDW, LM, RF, RFK, and SRK. The SRK model shows high variability, peaking near 55 parts per million around 13700000 Easting. The OK model shows a smoother, lower trend, generally below 40 parts per million. Panel b, at the bottom, displays predicted cobalt concentration in parts per million on the vertical axis, ranging from 0 to 30, against Easting in metres on the horizontal axis, ranging from 13650000 to 13750000. Similar to panel a, the SRK model exhibits high variability, with peaks reaching over 30 parts per million. The OK model again shows a smoother, lower trend, generally below 20 parts per million. Both panels show similar relative trends among the six models, with SRK and RFK models exhibiting the most pronounced fluctuations.)
